  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Project\'s Scope**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the prompt\'s instructions, specifically those regarding file saving conventions. I\'m paying close attention to the specified directories, particularly how the design document fits into the broader structure. I\'m ensuring I accurately interpret the user\'s instructions for context and skill files.\n\n\n**Refining File Placement Strategy**\n\nI\'ve revised the file saving approach. Now, project documentation files (`DESIGN.md`, `PRD.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `TODO.md`) will be saved in both the `/.agents/` and `/.agents/skills/` directories. Additionally, I\'ll place the four skill files (`motion-and-animation.md`, `ui-polish-microinteractions.md`, `21st-and-library-integration.md`, and `high-end-visual-design.md`) in *both* `/.agents/` and `/.agents/skills/` to guarantee that they are accessible and organized, regardless of the target directory that the user may check. Also, I\'ve added a note that an optional \"Documentation/Architecture\" modal or drawer should be present in the application\'s footer.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Placeholder Design**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the user\'s explicit request regarding image generation. It\'s clear that I should *not* invoke `generate_image`. Instead, I\'ll focus on creating ultra-high-end, interactive UI mockup placeholders for the Anke VPN interface. This will include realistic Russian UI controls, protocol indicators, and a flexible space for the user to drop in their screenshots.\n\n\n**Defining the Visual Style**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the design specs for Anke VPN, paying close attention to the visual style and typography. I\'m focusing on the dark mode aesthetic, with specific color tokens and CSS variables, inspired by the noted references. I am diligently implementing the Google Fonts for both `Plus Jakarta Sans` and `JetBrains Mono` in `index.html`. My aim is to deliver a UI that meets the brutalist-premium palette demands, carefully avoiding purple AI gradients. I have a firm handle on the fluid clamping aspect as well.\n\n\n**Constructing the Top Bar**\n\nI\'m currently building the top bar contract with its three zones. I am ensuring the brand wordmark (\"Anke VPN\") is a clean, single-line text element. The four to five navigation links will have subtle hover underlines, and the primary action button will scroll to pricing or open a quick checkout modal. I\'m focusing on \"\320\222\320\276\320\267\320\274\320\276\320\266\320\275\320\276\321\201\321\202\320\270\", \"\320\237\320\273\320\260\321\202\321\204\320\276\321\200\320\274\321\213\", \"\320\230\320\275\321\204\321\200\320\260\321\201\321\202\321\200\321\203\320\272\321\202\321\203\321\200\320\260\", \"\320\242\320\260\321\200\320\270\321\204\321\213\", and \"\320\223\320\260\321\200\320\260\320\275\321\202\320\270\321\217\" for the links.\n\n\n\n**Designing the Right Sidebar**\n\nNow I\'m designing the right sidebar. I\'m focusing on a slightly tilted mockup of the Anke VPN app with interactive connection state, and a way for the user to upload their screenshot within the placeholder. It will use subtle scroll parallax effects. There is an additional cross-platform download section for app store, google play, windows, and linux. Each card will have subtle yellow glow effects.\n\n\n**Implementing Bento Grid**\n\nI am now implementing the Bento grid. I\'m focusing on \"\320\237\321\200\320\265\320\270\320\274\321\203\321\211\320\265\321\201\321\202\320\262\320\260\" with an asymmetrical grid. I\'m working to highlight speed up to 15 Gbit/s with a visualizer and live latency comparators, and emphasizing absolute privacy. There is also global access with high-capacity locations and smart split-tunneling.\n\n\n**Detailing the Proof Section**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Proof & Infrastructure Strip.\" I\'m focusing on key features such as access to essential services without speed loss, up to 10 devices simultaneously, and the fallback mechanisms for DPI-blocking (VLESS-Reality, WireGuard-obfs, and Shadowsocks-2022). All cards are being built with the \"Double-Bezel\" nested architecture. Additionally, I\'m including a screenshot showcase placeholder where users can drop in desktop and mobile screenshots. Finally, I am including verifiable uptime and peak throughput data.\n\n\n**Elaborating on Pricing Plans**\n\nI\'m deep into the pricing section. I\'ve got the billing period selector, \"\320\237\320\276\320\264\320\277\320\270\321\201\320\272\320\260\" with its yellow highlight for individuals, and \"\320\230\320\275\320\264\320\270\320\262\320\270\320\264\321\203\320\260\320\273\321\214\320\275\320\276\" for dedicated servers, each within a Double-Bezel card. Clicking these opens a streamlined checkout modal. I\'m prioritizing user testimonials and metrics like \"< 19 ms average latency from Russia to Europe.\" I\'m including port details, access options, and device limits.\n\n\n**Finalizing Support Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"\320\223\320\260\321\200\320\260\320\275\321\202\320\270\321\217\" and support features. I am implementing a clear 30-day money-back guarantee with an FAQ accordion. The focus is on connection stability and speed. I\'ve engineered a global, floating support chat widget with lazy-loaded scripts and an interactive drawer for direct messaging and fast response times. I\'m also ensuring the payment method details are available to be specified for the user.\n\n\n"
