  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining VPN Data Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the core data for the Anke VPN components. I\'m building `/src/data/vpnData.ts` to manage platform-specific information: versions, system requirements, and direct download filenames. This clean, structured data will be essential for creating modular, polished components across various platforms.\n\n\n**Expanding Data & Components**\n\nI\'ve expanded the data structure to incorporate server locations for the Hero mockup and speed benchmark, including latency, port capacity, and protocols. Pricing plans and guarantee & FAQ items are also in the mix. On the component side, I\'m fleshing out the `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` component to adhere to the Top Bar Contract, complete with responsive mobile menu functionality. Furthermore, I\'ve got the Hero mockup\'s dynamic VPN interface placeholder in `/src/components/HeroMockup.tsx` underway, featuring parallax effects.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Interactions**\n\nI\'m now refining the interactive mockup component. There will be two selectable modes in the Hero\'s corner: interactive and screenshot upload. The interactive mode enables VPN connection toggling, server switching with latency displayed, and protocol selection. The screenshot slot offers a placeholder with dimensions and an upload button for local files, with support for PNG, JPG, and WebP formats.\n\n\n**Developing Download Modal**\n\nI\'m currently working on the interactive download / setup modal, which will appear on click. It will offer a 1-click download trigger, a Linux CLI copy command, and a VLESS/WireGuard key import guide. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s user-friendly and provides quick access to setup instructions.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features. Split-tunneling for localized services and support for HTTPS traffic to bypass DPI are in progress. I\'ve also added a 42+ location global access with up to 10 devices per account, alongside a dual-device screenshot gallery where users can preview uploaded screenshots. I\'m building `/src/components/PricingSection.tsx` to include tactile subscription cards, a billing cycle selector, and the 30-day money-back guarantee with FAQ. Finally, I\'ve got `/src/components/CheckoutModal.tsx` in development for the subscription purchase and dedicated node configuration, with payment selection.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4962152704875633973"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface ServerNode {\\n  id: string;\\n  city: string;\\n  country: string;\\n  code: string;\\n  pingMs: number;\\n  speedGbps: number;\\n  loadPercent: number;\\n  protocol: \'VLESS-Reality\' | \'WireGuard\' | \'Shadowsocks-2022\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface PlatformItem {\\n  id: \'ios-macos\' | \'android\' | \'windows\' | \'linux\';\\n  name: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  version: string;\\n  requirements: string;\\n  badgeText: string;\\n  fileName: string;\\n  fileSize: string;\\n  cliCommand?: string;\\n  steps: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport const SERVER_NODES: ServerNode[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: \'fi-hel\',\\n    city: \'\320\245\320\265\320\273\321\214\321\201\320\270\320\275\320\272\320\270\',\\n    country: \'\320\244\320\270\320\275\320\273\321\217\320\275\320\264\320\270\321\217\',\\n    code: \'FI-HEL-01\',\\n    pingMs: 14,\\n    speedGbps: 14.8,\\n    loadPercent: 24,\\n    protocol: \'VLESS-Reality\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'de-fra\',\\n    city: \'\320\244\321\200\320\260\320\275\320\272\321\204\321\203\321\200\321\202\',\\n    country: \'\320\223\320\265\321\200\320\274\320\260\320\275\320\270\321\217\',\\n    code: \'DE-FRA-04\',\\n    pingMs: 18,\\n    speedGbps: 15.0,\\n    loadPercent: 31,\\n    protocol: \'VLESS-Reality\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'nl-ams\',\\n    city: \'\320\220\320\274\321\201\321\202\320\265\321\200\320\264\320\260\320\274\',\\n    country: \'\320\235\320\270\320\264\320\265\321\200\320\273\320\260\320\275\320\264\321\213\',\\n    code: \'NL-AMS-02\',\\n    pingMs: 22,\\n    speedGbps: 14.6,\\n    loadPercent: 28,\\n    protocol: \'WireGuard\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'pl-waw\',\\n    city: \'\320\222\320\260\321\200\321\210\320\260\320\262\320\260\',\\n    country: \'\320\237\320\276\320\273\321\214\321\210\320\260\',\\n    code: \'PL-WAW-01\',\\n    pingMs: 16,\\n    speedGbps: 14.2,\\n    loadPercent: 19,\\n    protocol: \'VLESS-Reality\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'ch-zrh\'