  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Website Copy**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the official website\'s copy at `https://anke.dev/vnp/ru/`, starting with the logo and navigation. I\'ve downloaded the official logo from `https://anke.dev/vpn/icons/Logo.svg` for a closer look. I\'m focusing on the clarity and conciseness of the text, string by string.\n\n\n**Implementing Visuals and Links**\n\nOkay, I\'m now working on the logo, which I\'ve saved locally. I\'ll render the SVG inline within the header and hero sections. Regarding the navigation, I have determined the links, which include \'\320\223\320\273\320\260\320\262\320\275\320\260\321\217\', \'\320\241\320\277\320\270\321\201\320\276\320\272 \321\201\320\265\321\200\320\262\320\265\321\200\320\276\320\262\', \'\320\246\320\265\320\275\321\213\', and \'\320\237\320\276\320\264\320\264\320\265\321\200\320\266\320\272\320\260\'. For the header action, the button will lead to the app at the specified URL. The hero section is next, with its title, subtitle, and primary button copy now defined, along with the visual placeholder design.\n\n\n**Defining Download Section**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the \"Cross-Platform Download\" section. I\'ve got the title and subtitle copy down pat. I\'m building out the card structure, including the links for App Store, Google Play, and Windows. I\'m focusing on making the dropdown menus for Windows and Linux interactive and ensuring the provided links are accurate.\n\n\n**Constructing Bento Grid Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Bento Grid section, focusing on the three core features. I\'ve got the exact titles and text ready for each: \'\320\241\320\272\320\276\321\200\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\214\', \'\320\237\321\200\320\270\320\262\320\260\321\202\320\275\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\214\', and \'\320\224\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\203\320\277\320\275\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\214\'. I\'m designing interactive visuals for each, like an animated 15 Gbit/s fiber stream with a speed gauge, and a zero-trace animation. The goal is a highly engaging, asymmetrical layout with placeholder screenshots to be filled.\n\n\n**Visualizing Server Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the \"\320\224\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\203\320\277\320\275\320\276\321\201\321\202\321\214\" feature within the Bento Grid. I have the title and text locked down. My primary focus is on an interactive animation: a live grid representing the eight official servers, complete with real flag icons and specific city names. I\'m working on making each element interactive, building that real-time visual connection to the servers.\n\n\n**Designing Pricing Plans**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the pricing section, starting with the exact official copy for \"\320\222\320\260\321\200\320\270\320\260\320\275\321\202\321\213 \320\277\320\276\320\264\320\277\320\270\321\201\320\276\320\272.\" I\'m creating two distinct cards. The first card is for standard subscriptions, outlining the features and monthly pricing, and linking to the purchase page. The second card is for individual subscriptions, with details on custom terms, and direct inquiry link.\n\n\n**Finalizing Site Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final sections. In the \"Refund\" banner, I\'m using the exact copy \"\320\222\320\276\320\267\320\262\321\200\320\260\321\202 \320\262 \321\202\320\265\321\207\320\265\320\275\320\270\320\265 15 \320\264\320\275\320\265\320\271,\" with a description emphasizing the straightforward refund policy. For the \"Support\" section, I\'ve got the title and subtitle, and am implementing the three support cards. These cards will link to the live chat, Telegram support, and email. The live chat card will directly open the chat widget. I\'m focusing on seamless user experience across all of these elements. I\'m setting the stage for the final review.\n\n\n**Adding Footer and Animations**\n\nI\'ve just added the footer with its links and copyright information. Now, I\'m focusing on rich animations, inspired by several sites. I\'m working on interactive spotlight cursors for all cards and a 3D spring tilt effect for the Hero section\'s interface mockup, enhancing the site\'s visual appeal.\n\n\n**Refining Interactions and Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive elements. In the speed card, I\'m implementing animated light beams along fiber lines with a spring-physics-driven speedometer and digital counter. For server connectivity, I\'m working on animating a connection wave upon clicking any server, with real-time updates. The Hero section\'s entrance will use a blurred-to-crisp effect and spring-physics for a smooth introduction. I\'m updating the data file with authentic information.\n\n\n"
