  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mantle and App**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the provided images, specifically focusing on `IMG_4395_31872753.JPG` and `IMG_4396_3f997e9b.JPG`, which appear to depict Anke\'s **Mantle** protocol and **iPhone app interface**. The images provide authentic data and visual design aspects. The analysis is ongoing, and my focus is the app\'s key features.\n\n\n**Comparing Efficiency Metrics**\n\nI\'m now diving into the benchmark data presented. It\'s a direct comparison of Anke\'s Mantle and Happ\'s VLESS, contrasting performance metrics on iPhone and Android. I\'m focusing on the significant differences in energy consumption and CPU usage. The yellow bars represent Mantle, and the gray bars represent VLESS. So far, the results are really interesting.\n\n\n**Evaluating Performance Benchmarks**\n\nI\'m now deep into comparing Mantle\'s performance metrics against Happ\'s VLESS. Specifically, I\'m noting significant memory differences. On the iPhone, Mantle uses roughly 5MB versus VLESS\'s approximate 50MB. On Android, Mantle uses 21MB against VLESS\'s 103MB. Additionally, Mantle is around 2.2 times faster opening websites on iPhone and 2.1 times faster on Android, per the provided median data. I am using the devices referenced in the footer note to make these comparisons.\n\n\n**Observing App Features**\n\nI\'ve just focused on the bottom tab bar of the iPhone app; it\'s quite clear. It has three tabs: Home, Regions, and Settings. The Regions screen specifically, titled \"\320\241\320\277\320\270\321\201\320\276\320\272 \321\201\320\265\321\200\320\262\320\265\321\200\320\276\320\262,\" features a \"\320\237\321\200\320\265\320\274\320\270\321\203\320\274 \321\201\320\265\321\200\320\262\320\265\321\200\321\213\" subheader and a list of servers with country flags, city names, and active server indicators. I\'m noting the clear visual cues for active servers, the use of a yellow dot, and the added badge for Albania.\n\n\n**Examining UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the iPhone app\'s \"\320\235\320\260\321\201\321\202\321\200\320\276\320\271\320\272\320\270\" screen, specifically the visual elements. I\'m noting the \"\320\222\320\260\321\210 \320\275\320\276\320\274\320\265\321\200\" section, the \"\320\237\320\276\320\264\320\277\320\270\321\201\320\272\320\260\" card with its distinct border, and the \"\320\223\320\264\320\265 \320\264\320\276\320\273\320\266\320\265\320\275 \321\200\320\260\320\261\320\276\321\202\320\260\321\202\321\214 Anke?\" section. I\'m also focusing on the utility cards at the bottom with their respective icons and text. The red \"\320\222\321\213\321\205\320\276\320\264\" button in the top right is also of note.\n\n\n**Constructing Dynamic Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the user\'s idea, and I\'m really excited. We\'re going to build a dynamic 3D iPhone showcase. I\'m focusing on the 3D iPhone 15 Pro Titanium model, including the bezel and Dynamic Island. I\'m focusing on implementing scroll-driven animations and interactive screen transitions to make it a great user experience. This includes a clear Mantle core indicator and one-tap connect toggle, ensuring functionality aligns with the visual appeal.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Stages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic 3D iPhone showcase, specifically its scroll-driven animations and screen transitions. I\'m prioritizing three authentic app screens: the \"\320\223\320\273\320\260\320\262\320\275\320\260\321\217\" stage with instant connection status, the \"\320\240\320\265\320\263\320\270\320\276\320\275\321\213\" screen replicating the server list UI, and the \"\320\235\320\260\321\201\321\202\321\200\320\276\320\271\320\272\320\270\" screen. The 3D model, using scroll functions, will morph through these stages, including the Mantle core indicator.\n\n\n**Implementing Benchmark Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive `VLESS \320\277\321\200\320\276\321\202\320\270\320\262 Mantle` benchmark section. I\'m focusing on recreating the data from `IMG_4395_31872753.JPG`, specifically the headers, subtitles, and legends for Mantle (yellow) and VLESS (gray). I\'m incorporating an interactive platform filter for both iPhone and Android comparisons, with scroll-triggered, spring-animated bars to show performance. I\'m prioritizing accuracy to the original data.\n\n\n**Visualizing Performance Ratios**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed performance comparisons from the benchmarks, making them interactive and visually engaging. I\'m focusing on exact ratio displays for Energy, Idle CPU, CPU per 1GB, VPN Tunnel Memory, and Website Opening Time. I\'m ensuring accurate iPhone vs. Android data presentation using clear visual cues, including hover tooltips that display the exact ratios. The visuals will be dynamic and accurate, based on the provided data, and I\'m using the devices noted in the footer as the basis for those values.\n\n\n"
