  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Choice**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on dissecting that CSS selector the user provided. My initial analysis is underway, and I am zeroing in on the specific element the user has targeted. I am drilling down to discern the intended action or modification the user wishes to make based on this particular selector. My next step will be correlating this with the user\'s intent.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Empty Space**\n\nI\'ve traced the CSS selector `section#features > div > div > div:nth-of-type(4) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2)` to its corresponding component, `BentoFeatures.tsx`. It appears the target is the fourth BENTO card. Specifically, it\'s the second `div` within the `SpotlightShell` of that card, where the Russian phrase \"\320\237\320\273\320\265\320\271\321\201\321\205\320\276\320\273\320\264\320\265\321\200 \320\264\320\273\321\217 \321\201\320\272\321\200\320\270\320\275\" currently resides, indicating a placeholder. The user\'s observation of \"nothing\" seems correct, given that it\'s an empty placeholder.\n\n\n**Envisioning the Replacement**\n\nI\'m now formulating a plan to replace the placeholder in the fourth Bento card. My goal is to add a dynamic interface showing Anke\'s desktop and incorporate smart routing rules, along with a live monitor. This aims to fill the empty space with a visually engaging and interactive element, contrasting the existing emptiness.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
