    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requests**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the requested choreography, identifying it as an Apple/Awwwards-style scroll-linked hardware integration. I\'ve noted the presence of two `IPhone3DModel` instances \342\200\223 one in the Hero section and another in the Mantle section. I\'m focusing on the single, unified 3D iPhone component.\n\n\n**Refining Movement Trajectory**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the 3D iPhone\'s movement, specifically a parabolic trajectory. The goal is a smooth arc as it transitions from the Hero to the Mantle section. I\'m considering adjustments to the `x` and `rotate` properties alongside the `y` axis for a more dynamic feel. The key challenge lies in making the iPhone naturally pass *behind* the \"#platforms\" section, like a physical barrier; I\'m exploring CSS stacking contexts to achieve this layering effect.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Layering Depth**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Z-index stacking order to achieve the desired layering effect. I\'ve assigned z-indices to different sections: `#hero` at z-10, the iPhone layer at z-20 (with pointer events controlled), and `#platforms` at z-30 with an opaque background and shadow. This should allow the iPhone to naturally travel behind the `#platforms` section, emerging from underneath.\n\n\n**Pinning and Scrolling Logic**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how to handle the scroll pinning within the mantle section, and I\'m leaning toward a React and Framer Motion approach. The goal is to ensure pixel-perfect alignment between the Hero and Mantle sections, irrespective of screen size. The challenge is that the mantle section must pin and have scrollable elements within it. The key is in determining how best to trigger the final section scroll when the scrollable items are completed.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Smooth Transitions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the iPhone\'s behavior throughout the scrolling sections, focusing on how the Mantle sticky container functions. I\'m building a `<HeroToMantleChoreography />` component that encompasses distinct scrolling behaviors. This includes the placement and movement of the iPhone through the hero, the scroll track, and when unpinned from the mantle. I\'m ensuring smooth animation when it transitions from sticky to standard scroll behavior. I will ensure zero-jitter.\n\n\n**Mapping iPhone Transitions**\n\nI\'m now carefully mapping the single 3D iPhone\'s journey across all scrolling stages. I\'m focusing on the `#platforms` section, which has a z-index of 30, a dark background, and a shadow, ensuring the iPhone slides *underneath* it, emerging from the bottom. The `#mantle-track` section contains the sticky viewport, where the iPhone eventually lands. This includes the interactive step cards, progress indicators, and an anchor point for the iPhone in the right column. I need to ensure seamless transitions between all elements.\n\n\n**Tracing Scroll Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now tracing the iPhone\'s scroll-based position using two anchor slots: `heroSlotRef` and `mantleSlotRef`. I\'m tracking the behavior of `mantleSlotRef.getBoundingClientRect()` during the scrolling phases. In Phase A, I\'m analyzing the iPhone\'s viewport position relative to the Hero section until the Mantle track pins. I\'ll need `arrivalScrollY` to mark when the Mantle section reaches the top, and pins.\n\n\n**Calculating Scroll-Based Positions**\n\nI\'m now calculating the precise scroll positions and transition parameters for the iPhone. I\'m focusing on the relationship between `scrollY` and `arrivalScrollY`, the point where the Mantle section locks into place at the top of the viewport. As the iPhone transitions between Hero and Mantle, I\'m defining a normalized time variable `t` that represents the scroll progress. Currently, I\'m debating the effects of using document vs viewport coordinates for more natural layering under the #platforms section.\n\n\n**Defining Scroll Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now defining the scroll dynamics based on document and viewport coordinates. I\'ve pinpointed the key positions: the iPhone\'s start in the Hero, the Mantle track\'s pin point, and the `scrollY` values. Now I\'m focusing on the movement between those anchor points. I\'m exploring the iPhone\'s movement through the \"#platforms\" section (`z-30`, opaque background), which exists from `Y = 700px` to `Y = 1150px`, relative to document scroll position.\n\n\n**Refining Animation Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the animation logic, specifically the iPhone\'s behavior as it transitions under the `#platforms` section. My current focus is how the parabolic curve of the iPhone intersects with this section during scroll transitions. The goal is to make the iPhone visibly slide behind the platform seamlessly, then emerge as the user continues to scroll. I\'m focusing on Phase B, when `#mantle-track` is pinned.\n\n\n\n**Defining Pinned Scroll Behavior**\n\nI\'m now determining what happens within the pinned section. The Mantle track is sticky and doesn\'t move. The iPhone is locked to its Mantle slot. Subtle 3D rotation happens as the user scrolls, changing the iPhone screen content. I have defined 3 stages, with `\320\223\320\273\320\260\320\262\320\275\320\260\321\217`, `\320\240\320\265\320\263\320\270\320\276\320\275\321\213`, and `\320\235\320\260\321\201\321\202\321\200\320\276\320\271\320\272\320\270` content. The transition logic is now defined.\n\n\n**Verifying Mantle Unpinning**\n\nI\'ve just verified the math behind the Mantle section\'s unpinning and the iPhone\'s behavior. It seems the iPhone, post-pinned state, will seamlessly follow the Mantle slot as the section unpins and scrolls, effectively remaining parked. I\'m taking a moment to appreciate this elegant solution before moving on.\n\n\n**Calculating Travel Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now calculating the viewport coordinates of the iPhone during its travel phase before the Mantle section pins. I\'m focusing on the `scrollY` values in relation to the `arrivalScrollY`. I\'m using clamping to normalize the progress `t`. My thought is to then calculate the iPhone\'s `(x, y)` position relative to the document based on the `heroSlotRef` offset coordinates.\n\n\n**Determining Document vs. Viewport**\n\nI\'m now determining whether to use document or viewport coordinates, and I\'m currently leaning towards viewport coordinates. Analyzing `mantleSlotRef`\'s document Y coordinate at `scrollY = arrivalScrollY`, I\'m calculating the iPhone\'s `(x, y)` position relative to the document based on the `heroSlotRef` offset coordinates. I\'m focusing on Phase A when scrollY is from 0 to arrivalScrollY.\n\n\n**Mapping Parabolic Path**\n\nI\'m now mapping the iPhone\'s parabolic trajectory using a normalized time variable, *t*. The key is how the `parabola(t) = 4 * t * (1 - t)` function dictates the iPhone\'s viewport X position. The goal is to calculate the viewport X positions as it curves behind the `#platforms` section, at `t = 0.5` with `parabola(0.5) = 1`, and emerges at the Mantle section. I am calculating how much to offset the horizontal `arcOffsetX` coordinate value during the parabolic flight.\n\n\n**Defining iPhone Animations**\n\nI\'m now defining the scroll-based transformations for the iPhone\'s animation. I\'ve focused on rotation and scaling across key phases. Specifically, during flight, I\'m adjusting `rotateZ`, `rotateY`, `rotateX`, and `scale`. The key is to refine how it smoothly transitions to a pinned state within the Mantle.\n\n\n**Validating Slot Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now thinking I can measure `heroSlotRef.getBoundingClientRect()` and `mantleSlotRef.getBoundingClientRect()` directly on every animation frame or scroll update to validate the iPhone slot positions. The use of `getBoundingClientRect()` seems like a straightforward, foolproof solution.\n\n\n**Tracing Slot Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now tracing the viewport positions of both `heroSlotRef` and `mantleSlotRef` to ensure the iPhone\'s precise alignment throughout the scroll phases. I\'m focusing on their dynamic behavior, especially the stationary state of `mantleSlotRef` during the pinned section and its movement before. The use of `getBoundingClientRect()` should provide foolproof positions for the iPhone.\n\n\n**Refining Slot Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the slot positions and analyzing how they\'re affected by the `sticky top-0` parent. Specifically, the relationship between `mantleSlotRef` and its behavior. I\'m focusing on the automatic pinning and unpinning which is handled by CSS. I\'m leveraging the automatic pinning for precise coordination during transitions, and how the `sticky` parent influences the overall logic.\n\n\n**Verifying Zero Drift**\n\nI\'m now verifying the claim of zero drift and misalignment using viewport and document coordinates, specifically when the iPhone passes behind the `#platforms` section. The `lerp` function will allow smooth travel from `heroDocY` to `mantleDocY` in document coordinates, ensuring it passes behind the `#platforms` section. After the travel, it aligns with a `mantleSlot` inside a sticky section. No drift, misalignment, or jump is expected.\n\n\n**Calculating iPhone Layering**\n\nI\'m now calculating precise viewport coordinates to verify the iPhone\'s layering relative to the `#platforms` section during the scroll. Using a lerp function and analyzing the document coordinates, I have verified the iPhone appears partially behind `#platforms`. The iPhone is deep behind at `scrollY = 575px`, emerging at scrollY = 650.\n\n\n**Validating Parabolic Arc**\n\nI\'m now validating the parabolic arc calculation, specifically the iPhone\'s `(x, y)` position relative to viewport and document coordinates. After calculations for the `scrollY` values, I\'m verifying the layering in relation to the `#platforms` section. The calculations confirm precise viewport coordinate mapping, including accurate vertical travel, with the iPhone emerging from behind the `#platforms` section at the correct point, and landing smoothly in the Mantle section.\n\n\n**Validating Scroll Alignment**\n\nI\'m now validating the precise alignment of the iPhone\'s movements between the Hero and Mantle sections. I\'ve re-examined the parabolic curve with a focus on the `arcAmplitude` for a smooth horizontal offset. Using `heroRect.left` and `mantleRect.left`, I\'m confirming the visual positioning aligns within the right column of the container. I\'m ensuring smooth horizontal and vertical travel.\n\n\n**Validating Parabolic Flight**\n\nI\'m now validating the parabolic flight path with a particular focus on the `#platforms` section. The iPhone\'s movements from a parabolic dive inward, behind the section, and outward to the right is in question. The adjustments to `rotateZ`, `rotateY`, and `scale` for mobile need a precise implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Mantle**\n\nI\'m now integrating interactivity into the Mantle section. I\'m focusing on user clicks on steps \'01\', \'02\', and \'03\', which should scroll the view to the relevant position while simultaneously changing the iPhone\'s screen. I also added a progress indicator. Furthermore, I\'m building a dedicated `<HeroMantleChoreography />` component.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
