    thinking: "**Verifying Pricing Displays**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `PricingSection.tsx` component. I\'ve confirmed that, when the region is set to \'cis\', the display shows \"199 \342\202\275\" for `activeTerm.perMonthDisplay`. The plan has additional pricing notes.\n\n\n**Analyzing Regional Pricing**\n\nI\'ve examined the conditional rendering within the `PricingSection.tsx` component. Specifically, when the region is \'cis\', it displays \"199 \342\202\275 / \320\274\320\265\321\201\321\217\321\206\" with additional notes, suggesting a distinct pricing model for the CIS region. The component toggles different pricing terms based on the current region.\n\n\n**Investigating UI Updates**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI updates related to the term selection buttons within the pricing section. I\'m focusing on the visual cues for active and inactive states and the transitions between them, particularly the `className` logic within the component, specifically the style applied when the button is active. I see the classes are applying styles based on state. I\'m checking the hover states to make sure the interactions feel intuitive.\n\n\n**Confirming Pricing Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on the pricing logic for the \'global\' region within `PricingSection.tsx`. I\'ve verified the component correctly displays prices based on the user\'s term selection, ranging from one month to twelve months. I confirmed discounts are also correctly applied and displayed (e.g., \342\210\22210%). I\'m now cross-referencing these displays with the expected values to ensure consistency in total plan price and per-month clarity.\n\n\n**Reviewing Global Price Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the official price display for the \'global\' region within the `PricingSection.tsx` component. I see the price display is conditionally rendered. I\'m focusing on the `activeTerm.priceDisplay` element and associated labels, and how the monthly price is displayed in relation to the overall term. I\'m ensuring it\'s displaying appropriately and intuitively.\n\n\n"
