  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Smooth Scroll**\n\nI\'ve discovered HTML now supports `scroll-behavior: smooth;`! My focus has shifted to inspecting the `scroll spy` logic within `App.tsx` to confirm its compatibility and smooth behavior, especially concerning the header offset when navigating via anchor links. I\'m checking how the browser scrolls to elements when the user clicks an anchor, such as `#mantle` or `#features`, in that file.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic to handle scrolling to the bottom. I\'m adjusting the `handleScroll` function to accurately highlight sections like \"support\" or \"pricing\" when the user nearly reaches the bottom of the page, even if the offset isn\'t exact. This involves checking if `window.innerHeight + window.scrollY` is within a small threshold of the document\'s total height, ensuring those sections are active when appropriate.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8499015149710560233"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Refine scroll spy detection for bottom of page in App.tsx\",\"EndLine\":48,\"Instruction\":\"Improve bottom-of-page check in scroll spy\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"    const handleScroll = () => {\\n      // Bottom of page detection (support section)\\n      if (window.innerHeight + window.scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 100) {\\n        setActiveSection(\'support\');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      // Top of page detection\\n      if (window.scrollY < 120) {\\n        setActiveSection(\'top\');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      const scrollPos = window.scrollY + 220; // Offset for header and mid-viewport detection\\n\\n      // Check sections from bottom to top\\n      for (let i = sectionIds.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n        const id = sectionIds[i];\\n        const el = document.getElementById(id);\\n        if (el) {\\n          const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n          const top = rect.top + window.scrollY;\\n          if (scrollPos >= top) {\\n            setActiveSection(id);\\n            return;\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      setActiveSection(\'top\');\\n    };\",\"StartLine\":17,\"TargetContent\":\"    const handleScroll = () => {\\n      const scrollPos = window.scrollY + 200; // Offset for header and comfortable detection\\n\\n      // If at very top\\n      if (window.scrollY < 100) {\\n        setActiveSection(\'top\');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check sections from bottom to top\\n      for (let i = sectionIds.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n        const id = sectionIds[i];\\n        const el = document.getElementById(id);\\n        if (el) {\\n          const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n          const top = rect.top + window.scrollY;\\n          if (scrollPos >= top) {\\n            setActiveSection(id);\\n            return;\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      setActiveSection(\'top\');\\n    };\",